;; masago 真砂 — seed open-materials graph (real, PUBLIC computed-materials data only)
;; ADR-2606151027 · vocabulary: open-materials-ontology (00-contracts/schemas/open-materials-ontology.kotoba.edn)
;;
;; SCOPE GUARD (constitutional, G1 — read first):
;;   - masago is a RESEARCH map of PUBLIC computed-materials data, NEVER a weapons-design or
;;     synthesis-recipe tool. It mirrors computed PROPERTIES + crystal STRUCTURES only. NO
;;     synthesis route, NO precursor list, NO enrichment/processing procedure appears here —
;;     those fields are structurally unrepresentable (not schema members).
;;   - Weaponizable application classes are NOT enum members. Dual-use materials are mirrored at
;;     the property level only. The routing is open research, never fabrication or force (§1.12).
;;   - The lens is integrated discovery EVIDENCE over a material, routed to RESEARCH. karma lives
;;     ONLY on edges (:en/grasping-load × disclosed :en/confidence; N1). The raw computed VALUE
;;     rides the edge as :en/value (DISCLOSED fact, never re-judged; N3).
;;
;; SOURCING: structures + computed properties are :authoritative publicly-disclosed facts from the
;;   open-materials commons — Meta FAIR Chemistry Open Materials 2024 (OMat24, CC-BY-4.0), the
;;   Materials Project (CC-BY-4.0), OQMD, NOMAD, AFLOW, JARVIS. The SAMPLE is a bounded illustrative
;;   seed (:representative coverage), NOT exhaustive: coverage of the ~10^8-scale commons is ~0 by
;;   design. mp-* source-ids are real Materials Project identifiers. Live ingest (Materials Project
;;   REST / OMat24 dumps) is G7/Council-gated. Property values are DISCLOSED DFT/MLIP results, never
;;   masago adjudications (N3).
;;
;; A NOTE ON VALUES: :en/value is a DISCLOSED computed number for orientation; it is NOT used in the
;;   discovery integral (which uses only :en/grasping-load × confidence). Precise re-verification of
;;   each datum against the source release is an R1 ingest task (live leg, G7).

